{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): PreactDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncer.ts#L163","children":[{"type":"text","value":"debouncer/useDebouncer.ts:163"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Preact hook that creates and manages a Debouncer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a lower-level hook that provides direct access to the Debouncer's functionality without\nany built-in state management. This allows you to integrate it with any state management solution\nyou prefer (useState, Redux, Zustand, etc.)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook provides debouncing functionality to limit how often a function can be called,\nwaiting for a specified delay before executing the latest call. This is useful for handling\nfrequent events like window resizing, scroll events, or real-time search inputs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debouncer.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canLeadingExecute"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have been completed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastArgs"},{"type":"text","value":": The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"unmount-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmount behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the hook cancels any pending execution when the component unmounts.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const debouncer = useDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactDebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactDebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactDebouncer.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactDebouncer"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<searchDebouncer.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })}>\n  {({ isPending }) => (\n    <div>{isPending ? 'Searching...' : 'Ready'}</div>\n  )}\n</searchDebouncer.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when isPending changes at hook level (optimized for loading states)\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when executionCount changes (optimized for tracking execution)\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Multiple state properties - re-render when any of these change\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isPending: state.isPending,\n    executionCount: state.executionCount,\n    status: state.status\n  })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = (e) => {\n  searchDebouncer.maybeExecute(e.target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending } = searchDebouncer.state;","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"unmount-behavior","text":"Unmount behavior","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): PreactDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/useDebouncer.ts:163](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncer.ts#L163)\n\nA Preact hook that creates and manages a Debouncer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level hook that provides direct access to the Debouncer's functionality without\nany built-in state management. This allows you to integrate it with any state management solution\nyou prefer (useState, Redux, Zustand, etc.).\n\nThis hook provides debouncing functionality to limit how often a function can be called,\nwaiting for a specified delay before executing the latest call. This is useful for handling\nfrequent events like window resizing, scroll events, or real-time search inputs.\n\nThe debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:\n\n**1. Using `debouncer.Subscribe` HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)**\n\nUse the `Subscribe` HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components.\n\n**2. Using the `selector` parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)**\n\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the `Subscribe` HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Unmount behavior\n\nBy default, the hook cancels any pending execution when the component unmounts.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst debouncer = useDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`PreactDebouncer`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncer.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<searchDebouncer.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })}>\n  {({ isPending }) => (\n    <div>{isPending ? 'Searching...' : 'Ready'}</div>\n  )}\n</searchDebouncer.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when isPending changes at hook level (optimized for loading states)\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when executionCount changes (optimized for tracking execution)\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Multiple state properties - re-render when any of these change\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isPending: state.isPending,\n    executionCount: state.executionCount,\n    status: state.status\n  })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = (e) => {\n  searchDebouncer.maybeExecute(e.target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending } = searchDebouncer.state;\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useDebouncer\ntitle: useDebouncer\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): PreactDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/useDebouncer.ts:163](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncer.ts#L163)\n\nA Preact hook that creates and manages a Debouncer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level hook that provides direct access to the Debouncer's functionality without\nany built-in state management. This allows you to integrate it with any state management solution\nyou prefer (useState, Redux, Zustand, etc.).\n\nThis hook provides debouncing functionality to limit how often a function can be called,\nwaiting for a specified delay before executing the latest call. This is useful for handling\nfrequent events like window resizing, scroll events, or real-time search inputs.\n\nThe debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:\n\n**1. Using `debouncer.Subscribe` HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)**\n\nUse the `Subscribe` HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components.\n\n**2. Using the `selector` parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)**\n\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the `Subscribe` HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions that have been completed\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending')\n\n## Unmount behavior\n\nBy default, the hook cancels any pending execution when the component unmounts.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst debouncer = useDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`PreactDebouncer`](../interfaces/PreactDebouncer.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<searchDebouncer.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })}>\n  {({ isPending }) => (\n    <div>{isPending ? 'Searching...' : 'Ready'}</div>\n  )}\n</searchDebouncer.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when isPending changes at hook level (optimized for loading states)\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when executionCount changes (optimized for tracking execution)\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ executionCount: state.executionCount })\n);\n\n// Multiple state properties - re-render when any of these change\nconst searchDebouncer = useDebouncer(\n  (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isPending: state.isPending,\n    executionCount: state.executionCount,\n    status: state.status\n  })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = (e) => {\n  searchDebouncer.maybeExecute(e.target.value);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { isPending } = searchDebouncer.state;\n```\n"}
